doc Print an int, u8, bool or str, followed by a newline.
  ```
  print 42
  print "hello"
  print 2 < 3      // true
  print 'A'        // 65
  ```

  Each `print` is one or two `write` system calls, so printing in a tight
  loop is dominated by system call cost.

syntax statement
  print {value: expr}
